diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 9fb62ad..8750098 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- C++ calls through a receiver resolve by its declared or inferred type, so `fox code Engine.start --rel callers` no longer marks them as guesses by name when several classes have a `start`: a local (`Engine e;`), a parameter (`Pump* p`, `const Pump& p`), a range-`for` variable, a member of a typed struct (`r.engine.start()`, `this->pump_->start()`, a bare `engine_.start()` inside a method), `auto` from `Engine()`, `new Pump` or `std::make_unique<Pump>()`, casts, and `typedef`/`using` aliases. `.` on a smart pointer, a library type or an undeclared receiver stays a guess. A method declared in its class is a prototype that stands for its out-of-line definition. C++ files parse again once (store schema 25).
 - `callers` of a C function-pointer member lists the lines storing a function in it (`.irq_mask = foo_mask,`) as their own group after the call sites, `stores a function in it (not calls): N`, no longer among the references that are not calls, and they no longer make the answer read as incomplete. `callers` of a function counts the documentation lines naming it after the verdict (`plus N in docs (not code, not listed)`) and never lists them.
 - The SubagentStart brief no longer carries the swarm board protocol line by default: in A/B runs it gave parallel subagents nothing and cost more. `[hooks] swarm_board = true` in `config.toml` brings it back. The parent packet and parent read lines stay.
 
