@@ -25,6 +25,23 @@ members, and those whose type path passes through a field or function whose type
 type path when a typedef changed). A run that re-parses most of a big project drops the old rows
 in one pass per table and resolves everything again.
 
+**C++ member calls.** A call through a receiver (`e.start()`, `p->start()`, `r.engine.start()`)
+stores the receiver as a type path like C's, with `T:Class` the one kind of type (C++ has no
+separate tag namespace) and each member after the base carrying its access operator (`.f`, `>f`
+for `->f`). The base is the declared type of a local, parameter (by value, pointer or
+reference), range-`for` variable or file-level variable, or the type `auto` takes from its
+initializer: `Engine()` or `Engine{}` (`K:Engine`: a constructor, or a function of that name
+whose return type is known), `new Pump`, `std::make_unique<Pump>()` and the casts. `this` (`H:`)
+and a bare name that is no local (`engine_.start()`) are the calling method's class and its data
+member. Types go through `typedef` and `using`. Smart pointers (`unique_ptr`, `shared_ptr`,
+`optional`) are `P:Class`: only `->` reaches the pointee, `.` reaches the pointer's own members and
+leaves the type unknown. Resolution reads the path to the receiver's class names (and what
+they are typedefs of) and takes the method of that class among the name's definitions: certain
+with one definition (a prototype in the class stands for its definition; overloads in one file are one),
+a guess among several same-name classes. A receiver whose type is unknown, a class the index has no such method
+for (a library type, a method of a base class), or a name-only chain stays scored by name, as
+before. Schema 25 parses C++ files again once.
+
 **Change detection on big trees** (`walkcache`). A tree of at least 50,000 files keeps its last
 walk in `$FOXDB_HOME/walk/<project id>`: the directories it entered with their modification
 times (nanoseconds), the files in each with size and mtime, the notes on directories it left out,
